{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015wDG7CPKDUZPTyZ6vpCzck","type":"tool_result","content":"280\t  id       String    @id @default(auto()) @map(\"_id\") @db.Objectid\n281\t  // Other fields\n282\t  comments Comment[] // A post can have many comments // [!code highlight]\n283\t}\n284\t\n285\tmodel Comment {\n286\t  id     String @id @default(auto()) @map(\"_id\") @db.Objectid\n287\t  // Other fields\n288\t  post   Post   @relation(fields: [postId], references: [id]) // A comment can have one post // [!code highlight]\n289\t  postId String @db.ObjectId\n290\t}\n291\t```\n292\t\n293\tRefer to the [relations documentation](/orm/v7/prisma-schema/data-model/relations) for more examples and information about relationships between models.\n294\t\n295\t### Native types mapping\n296\t\n297\t**Native database type attributes** describe the underlying database type:\n298\t\n299\t```prisma\n300\tmodel Post {\n301\t  id      Int    @id\n302\t  title   String @db.VarChar(200)\n303\t  content String\n304\t}\n305\t```\n306\t\n307\tType attributes are:\n308\t\n309\t- Specific to the underlying provider (e.g., PostgreSQL uses `@db.Boolean`, MySQL uses `@db.TinyInt(1)`)\n310\t- Written in PascalCase and prefixed by `@db`\n311\t- Only added during [introspection](/orm/v7/prisma-schema/introspection) if the native type differs from the default\n312\t\n313\tSee [native database type attributes](/orm/v7/reference/prisma-schema-reference#model-field-scalar-types) for the complete list.\n314\t\n315\t### Type modifiers\n316\t\n317\tThe type of a field can be modified by appending either of two modifiers:\n318\t\n319\t- [`[]`](/orm/v7/reference/prisma-schema-reference#-modifier) Make a field a list\n320\t- [`?`](/orm/v7/reference/prisma-schema-reference#-modifier-1) Make a field optional\n321\t\n322\t> **Note**: You **cannot** combine type modifiers - optional lists are not supported.\n323\t\n324\t#### Lists"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b5a8b5a-c7f1-4138-b1ed-a8d4ff393bc8","uuid":"939c6d52-53ae-47aa-946e-e655862b707b","timestamp":"2026-09-27T09:29:23.474Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jcarr/.cache/markdownattractor/bench/t4/qmd/src/apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v7/prisma-schema/data-model/models.mdx","content":"  id       String    @id @default(auto()) @map(\"_id\") @db.Objectid\n  // Other fields\n  comments Comment[] // A post can have many comments // [!code highlight]\n}\n\nmodel Comment {\n  id     String @id @default(auto()) @map(\"_id\") @db.Objectid\n  // Other fields\n  post   Post   @relation(fields: [postId], references: [id]) // A comment can have one post // [!code highlight]\n  postId String @db.ObjectId\n}\n```\n\nRefer to the [relations documentation](/orm/v7/prisma-schema/data-model/relations) for more examples and information about relationships between models.\n\n### Native types mapping\n\n**Native database type attributes** describe the underlying database type:\n\n```prisma\nmodel Post {\n  id      Int    @id\n  title   String @db.VarChar(200)\n  content String\n}\n```\n\nType attributes are:\n\n- Specific to the underlying provider (e.g., PostgreSQL uses `@db.Boolean`, MySQL uses `@db.TinyInt(1)`)\n- Written in PascalCase and prefixed by `@db`\n- Only added during [introspection](/orm/v7/prisma-schema/introspection) if the native type differs from the default\n\nSee [native database type attributes](/orm/v7/reference/prisma-schema-reference#model-field-scalar-types) for the complete list.\n\n### Type modifiers\n\nThe type of a field can be modified by appending either of two modifiers:\n\n- [`[]`](/orm/v7/reference/prisma-schema-reference#-modifier) Make a field a list\n- [`?`](/orm/v7/reference/prisma-schema-reference#-modifier-1) Make a field optional\n\n> **Note**: You **cannot** combine type modifiers - optional lists are not supported.\n\n#### Lists","numLines":45,"startLine":280,"totalLines":703}}}
